  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Scenery: Dutch clouds and trees conversing in intimate landscapes of their own. Mood of speech: the potential mood. Stage for this play: the spread, being both one and two."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Mood: Potential is a short artist book that was printed by Brad Freeman with assistance of Daniel Mellis at the Center for Book &amp; Paper Arts in Chicago. It was printed in duotone, referencing the two-part composites of each spread. The book stages and un-stages potential landscapes of clouds and trees in a discontinuous, jittery movement"--Artists' website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Dulcet, letterpress on cover and colophon. The book comes in an enclosure with the title printed in letterpress"--Artists' website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The book was included in the Journal of Artists' Books no 27.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Condition: no library markings, in protective enclosure.</subfield>
  </datafield>
